	"hardwareControls": [
		"Master: Volume, Tempo, Memory, Play, Record, Function",
		"VCO: Octave, Pitch 1, Pitch 2, Pitch 3, VCO 1, VCO 2, VCO 3",
		"Filter: Cutoff, Peak, EG intensity",
		"LFO: Rate, Intensity",
		"Envelope: Attack, Decay Release"
	],
	"notice": "Most controls are MIDI receive mappings. The unmodified hardware has no MIDI output and cannot send panel movements or notes to Harmoneasy. Cutoff and Peak are analog-only controls: they have no MIDI CC. Slide time CC5, expression CC11 and gate time CC49 are MIDI-only parameters and are not represented as physical knobs.  GUI controls generate MIDI into the chain; route that chain to a MIDI output to control the hardware. DIN devices normally appear under the MIDI interface name, so select the profile manually. Unmapped physical buttons and switches have stable SVG IDs for future bindings. Positions are schematic. Note surfaces use virtual defaults; use MIDI learn to match the hardware octave or configuration.",
